1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
When disaster strikes beneath dense monsoon clouds,

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,400
optical satellites are blind. But Earth's surface never stops dancing.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,800
Enter NISAR: NASA and ISRO's L-band radar.

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:13,500
We track surface changes across eleven repeat passes at twelve-day orbit cycles.

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:17,200
In our interactive supercomputer, drag the swipe wipe to detect slope motion,

6
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:21,000
drape radar observations on 3D terrain, and test physical hypotheses.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Transform complex interferometry into an actionable Evidence Request Brief for local community preparedness.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Echoes of Rasuwa: Dancing with SAR.

